On Friday 04 February 2011 20:25:51 Alex Rozenshteyn wrote:
> 6.15)  na'e zei .a zei na'e zei by. livgyterbilma
>        non-A, non-B liver-disease
>        non-A, non-B hepatitis
>
> 6.17)  na'e zei .a zei na'e zei by. zei livgyterbilma
>        non-A-non-B-hepatitis
>
> Shouldn't the {.a}s be {.abu}s?
>
> It seems to me that {na'e zei .a} refers to a logical connective that is
> not "or".

"na'e zei .abu zei na'e zei by" parses differently in jbofi'e than in camxes. 
In jbofi'e it's a tanru consisting of "na'e zei .a" and "bu zei na'e zei by". 
In camxes, if I'm reading the tree right, "na'e zei .a" is a lujvo, which is 
then converted into a letteral with "bu", then joined by "zei" to "na'e zei 
by".

